# .cursorrules - Project AI Coding Rules for Rolling Ball 3D (Awesome-Cursorrules)

## General Guidelines
- Write modern, clean, efficient HTML5 / CSS3 / ES6+ JavaScript.
- Prioritize high visual aesthetics, sleek dark modes, vibrant colors, and smooth 60+ FPS animations.
- Shortest working diff wins; avoid unnecessary dependencies and complex abstractions (Ponytail / YAGNI).

## Three.js & WebGL Best Practices
- **Garbage Collection Optimization**: Never allocate new `THREE.Vector3`, `THREE.Color`, or `THREE.Matrix4` inside `requestAnimationFrame` loops. Preallocate and reuse static buffers.
- **Resource Disposal**: Always call `dispose()` on geometries, materials, and textures when destroying or resetting 3D objects to prevent GPU memory leaks.
- **Object Pooling**: Implement Object Pools (`acquire()` and `recycle()`) for dynamic entities (tiles, particles, bursts, trails).
- **Lighting & Materials**: Use `MeshStandardMaterial` / `MeshPhysicalMaterial` with proper emissive lighting and environment maps for premium visual depth.

## Audio & Rhythm Mechanics
- Use Web Audio API (`AudioContext`, `BiquadFilterNode`, `AnalyserNode`) for low-latency audio processing.
- Maintain millisecond-precision offset calibration between AudioContext clock and 3D visual track movement.
